\begin{abstract}
Cyber-Physical Hydrocryptic Dynamics (CHD) is a trans-domain scientific discipline
that unifies real-time hydrodynamics, autonomous bifurcation intelligence,
structural impact physics, and post-quantum cryptographic verification into a
single operational framework. This white sheet summarizes the global deployment
model, governing mathematical principles, and hydraulic displacement capacity of
the CEUME-class architecture.
\end{abstract}

\section{Discipline Definition}
Cyber-Physical Hydrocryptic Dynamics (CHD) studies hydraulic systems whose
physical state evolution is inseparably coupled to:
\begin{itemize}
  \item real-time fluid solvers (2D SWE, 3D Navier--Stokes),
  \item autonomous control and bifurcation logic,
  \item post-quantum cryptographic key encapsulation,
  \item distributed Merkle-ledger state commitments.
\end{itemize}

\section{Governing Fluid Mechanics}
\subsection{Shallow-Water Equations}
Depth-averaged free-surface flow is modeled by:
\begin{align}
  \frac{\partial h}{\partial t}
  + \frac{\partial (hu)}{\partial x}
  + \frac{\partial (hv)}{\partial y}
  &= q_r, \\
  \frac{\partial (hu)}{\partial t}
  + \frac{\partial}{\partial x}\left(hu^2 + \frac{1}{2} g h^2\right)
  + \frac{\partial (huv)}{\partial y}
  &= -g h S_{fx} + q_{mx}, \\
  \frac{\partial (hv)}{\partial t}
  + \frac{\partial (huv)}{\partial x}
  + \frac{\partial}{\partial y}\left(hv^2 + \frac{1}{2} g h^2\right)
  &= -g h S_{fy} + q_{my},
\end{align}
where $h$ is water depth, $(u,v)$ are depth-averaged velocities, $g$ is
gravitational acceleration, and $q_r$ represents rainfall/runoff sources.

\subsection{Froude Instability Criterion}
Local flow regime is classified via the Froude number:
\begin{equation}
  Fr = \frac{\lVert \mathbf{u} \rVert}{\sqrt{g h}},
\end{equation}
with $Fr \ge 1$ indicating supercritical flow and potential hydraulic jumps
triggering bifurcation control.

\section{Autonomous Bifurcation Control}
When instability is detected, execution splits into:
\begin{itemize}
  \item Baseline predictive routing (primary agent),
  \item Exploratory MPC sub-agent optimizing valve and pump states.
\end{itemize}
A local cost functional for inundation minimization is:
\begin{equation}
  J = \int_{\Omega} w(x,y)\, h(x,y,t)\, \mathrm{d}x\,\mathrm{d}y,
\end{equation}
subject to actuator and regulatory constraints, solved within a sub-frame
time budget to reconverge before the next global cycle.

\section{Cryptographic and Ledger Layer}
Post-quantum key encapsulation (e.g.\ CRYSTALS-Kyber) secures inter-node
channels, while AES-GCM-256 provides symmetric in-transit confidentiality.
Each simulation frame and control action is committed as a Merkle-tree leaf,
yielding an immutable audit trail:
\begin{equation}
  \text{Root} = H\big(H(s_1 \Vert s_2), H(s_3 \Vert s_4), \dots \big),
\end{equation}
where $H$ is a cryptographic hash and $s_i$ are state vectors or stress tensors.

\section{Hydraulic Displacement Capacity}
\subsection{Positive Displacement}
Deterministic volumetric throughput of pumps is:
\begin{equation}
  Q_{\text{pos}} = V_{\text{disp}} \cdot n_{\text{rpm}},
\end{equation}
with $V_{\text{disp}}$ the swept volume per revolution and $n_{\text{rpm}}$
the rotational speed.

\subsection{Hydrostatic Force Multiplication}
Pascal's law yields:
\begin{equation}
  \frac{F_2}{F_1} = \frac{A_2}{A_1},
\end{equation}
enabling hydraulic gates and barriers to amplify force without volumetric loss.

\subsection{Buoyant Displacement}
Archimedes' principle governs buoyant control elements:
\begin{equation}
  F_b = \rho_{\text{fluid}} g V_{\text{sub}},
\end{equation}
where $F_b$ is buoyant force, $\rho_{\text{fluid}}$ fluid density, and
$V_{\text{sub}}$ submerged volume.

